Linux System Calls.

Explanation:

System call - Purpose
open() - Opens or creates a file.
read() - Reads data from a file.
write() - Writes data into a file.
close() - Closes an opened file.
getpid() - Returns the current process ID.
getuid() - Returns the current user ID.
getgid() - Returns the current group ID.
lseek() - Changes the file pointer position.


Important concepts:

O_CREAT – Creates the file if it doesn't exist.
O_RDWR – Opens the file for reading and writing.
O_TRUNC – Clears existing file content.
0644 – Sets file permissions.
SEEK_SET – Moves the file pointer relative to the beginning.
